---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Legal from '../../components/Legal.astro';
import { EMPRESA, DPO } from '../../data/empresa';

const atualizado = 'October 16, 2026';
// RASCUNHO para revisão jurídica (Laura). Tradução EN da versão em português; a versão em português prevalece.
// Itens a confirmar marcados com TODO_ no código.
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | i9c"
  description="How i9c (IVM Telecomunicação) collects, uses, shares and protects your personal data on its website, under Brazil's LGPD."
  rota="politica-de-privacidade"
>
  <Legal eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy Policy" updated={atualizado} rota="politica-de-privacidade">
    <p>
      This Policy explains how <strong>{EMPRESA.razaoSocial}</strong> (CNPJ {EMPRESA.cnpj}), the company responsible for
      the <strong>i9c</strong> brand, processes the personal data of people who use the <strong>i9c.net.br</strong> website,
      in compliance with Brazil's General Data Protection Law (Law No. 13,709/2018, “LGPD”).
    </p>
    <div class="box">
      <p style="margin:0">
        <strong>Summary:</strong> we only collect what is needed to handle your request; website usage measurement only
        happens after you click “Accept all”; we do not sell your data; you can ask for access, correction or deletion at any time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who the controller is</h2>
    <p>
      {EMPRESA.razaoSocial}, CNPJ {EMPRESA.cnpj}, headquartered at {EMPRESA.endereco}. Data processed through the
      customer area (<a href={EMPRESA.areaCliente}>app.i9c.net.br</a>) and under the mobile service contract is also
      governed by the terms of your service agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What data we collect and why</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (LGPD)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Where">Number portability request</td>
          <td data-label="Data">Name or company name, CPF/CNPJ (Brazilian individual/company taxpayer ID), email, contact phone number, address, number(s) to be ported, current carrier, number of lines, identity document and the line holder's document (image/PDF) and, for companies, a list of numbers</td>
          <td data-label="Purpose">To review and carry out the portability request and the service subscription; to contact you about the request</td>
          <td data-label="Legal basis">Preliminary procedures and performance of a contract (Art. 7, V); consent recorded on the form (Art. 7, I); regulatory obligation (Art. 7, II)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Where">WhatsApp, phone and website chat</td>
          <td data-label="Data">Name, phone number and the content of the conversation</td>
          <td data-label="Purpose">To answer questions and handle sales and support</td>
          <td data-label="Legal basis">Preliminary procedures/performance of a contract (Art. 7, V) and legitimate interest (Art. 7, IX)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Where">Browsing (measurement cookies)</td>
          <td data-label="Data">Pages visited, traffic source, device and browser type, cookie identifiers</td>
          <td data-label="Purpose">To measure audience and the performance of the website and campaigns</td>
          <td data-label="Legal basis">Consent (Art. 7, I) — only after “Accept all”</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Where">Website operation</td>
          <td data-label="Data">IP address and technical request data; your choice in the cookie notice (stored in your browser)</td>
          <td data-label="Purpose">To deliver the pages, keep the site secure and remember your choice</td>
          <td data-label="Legal basis">Legitimate interest (Art. 7, IX)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>We do not request sensitive data through the website. Documents submitted for portability are used only to verify ownership of the line.</p>

    <h2>3. Cookies and measurement</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Tag Manager</strong> and Google measurement tools only after you click “Accept all” in the
      cookie notice. With “Essential only”, no measurement cookies are activated. Your choice is saved in your browser;
      to change it, clear the site data in your browser and the notice will appear again.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal data. We share only what is necessary with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Our partner network operator (MVNO) and the entity that administers number portability</strong>, to activate the line and carry out the portability;</li>
      <li><strong>Your current carrier</strong>, during the portability process;</li>
      <li><strong>Technology providers</strong>: Google (Tag Manager/measurement and website fonts), our customer service chat and CRM provider, WhatsApp/Meta (messaging), OpenStreetMap (maps in the coverage map) and hosting providers;</li>
      <li><strong>Authorities</strong> (including ANATEL, Brazil's telecommunications regulator, and the courts), when required by law or court order.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of these providers may process data outside Brazil. In such cases, the transfer follows the cases permitted
      by Art. 33 of the LGPD.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long we keep data</h2>
    <p>
      For as long as needed to fulfill the purpose (for example, completing the portability and maintaining the contract)
      and, after that, for the periods required by law or by telecommunications regulations, or for the defense of legal
      claims. Once these periods end, the data is deleted or anonymized.
      <!-- TODO_RETENCAO: se houver prazo interno definido para documentos de portabilidade não concluída, citar aqui. -->
    </p>

    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Data travels over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). Portability documents are kept in a restricted area, outside
      the public website, with access limited to the responsible team. No system is 100% invulnerable; if an incident
      with relevant risk occurs, we will notify you and the ANPD (Brazil's National Data Protection Authority), as
      required by the LGPD.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You may, at any time, request:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>confirmation that we process your data and access to it;</li>
      <li>correction of incomplete, inaccurate or outdated data;</li>
      <li>anonymization, blocking or deletion of unnecessary data or data processed in breach of the law;</li>
      <li>portability of your data to another provider;</li>
      <li>deletion of data processed based on consent, and withdrawal of consent;</li>
      <li>information about who we share your data with.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some data may be kept even after your request, when required by law or regulation.</p>

    <h2>8. Data Protection Officer (DPO) and contact</h2>
    {DPO.nome ? (
      <p>
        Data Protection Officer: <strong>{DPO.nome}</strong> — <a href={`mailto:${DPO.email}`}>{DPO.email}</a>.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        To exercise your rights or ask questions about this Policy, contact us at
        <strong> {EMPRESA.telefone}</strong> or via <a href={EMPRESA.whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a>,
        stating that the subject is <strong>data privacy</strong>.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>You may also file a complaint with Brazil's National Data Protection Authority (ANPD).</p>

    <h2>9. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this Policy. The date at the top shows the version in force; relevant changes will be highlighted on the website.</p>
  </Legal>
</Base>
